From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kefu Chai <k.chai@proxmox.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:31:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] osd/ECTransaction: truncate padded shards of legacy EC
 objects

Without EC optimizations, every shard of an EC object is padded to the
stripe boundary. After allow_ec_optimizations is set on the pool,
truncate() only shrinks the shards whose optimized size, computed from
the old object size, is larger than the new one. The other shards keep
the legacy padding, so scrub finds them too long and flags the object
inconsistent.

With 4+2 and 4K chunks, all six shards of a 20K object are 8K.
Truncate it to 16K, and shards 1-3 stay at 8K instead of 4K. RBD hits
this when a discard or write-zeroes reaches the end of an object,
since librbd sends that as a truncate. With more than m shards
flagged, "ceph pg repair" marks them all missing and the object ends
up unfound, while its data was fine.

So truncate the remaining shards to their new size as well. Objects
written with EC optimizations already have that size. Extending the
rollback clone to cover the padding instead doesn't work: the primary
doesn't know how long it is, and BlueStore rejects a clone_range past
the end of an object.

Fixes: https://tracker.ceph.com/issues/81915
Signed-off-by: Kefu Chai <k.chai@proxmox.com>

(cherry picked from commit 344c82f845f76017a0854cf3b6f9d3609b561131)

Conflicts:
	src/test/osd/TestBackendBasics.cc: dropped, tentacle does not have
	PGBackendTestFixture which the new tests are built on.
---
 src/osd/ECTransaction.cc | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/osd/ECTransaction.cc b/src/osd/ECTransaction.cc
index cd03849ed4d4..41bad83bf334 100644
--- a/src/osd/ECTransaction.cc
+++ b/src/osd/ECTransaction.cc
@@ -714,6 +714,19 @@ void ECTransaction::Generate::truncate() {
           start_align_next);
       }
     }
+
+    // Shards of objects written before EC optimizations are padded to the
+    // stripe. Trim that padding too. It is zeros past the end, so it needs no
+    // rollback.
+    for (auto &&[shard, t] : transactions) {
+      if (truncate_eset.contains(shard)) {
+        continue;
+      }
+      t.truncate(
+        coll_t(spg_t(pgid, shard)),
+        ghobject_t(oid, ghobject_t::NO_GEN, shard),
+        sinfo.object_size_to_shard_size(op.truncate->first, shard));
+    }
     rollback_extents.emplace_back(make_pair(clone_start, clone_end - clone_start));
     rollback_shards.emplace_back(clone_shards);
   }
